    "title": "PREP 2026 Block 1 Question 16",
    "scenario": "A 2-month-old infant presents with moderate respiratory distress, poor breastfeeding, and generalized weakness. His mother says he has never fed well and appears thin. He lies in a frog-leg position with absent deep tendon reflexes, prominent wasting of tongue, face, and jaw, and little spontaneous movement. Extraocular movements and pupillary reflexes are normal. BUN is mildly elevated and creatine kinase is normal. Which region marked in the schematic best explains these findings?",
