    "id": 9017,
    "title": "PREP 2026 Block 1 Question 17",
    "scenario": "A 13-month-old infant is evaluated one day after complete tetralogy of Fallot repair. He is sedated, ventilated, and receiving milrinone 0.5 µg/kg/min and epinephrine 0.05 µg/kg/min. Sinus tachycardia. Ventilator: tidal volume 6 mL/kg, PIP 25 cm H₂O, PEEP 8 cm H₂O, rate 30/min, inspiratory time 0.5 seconds, FiO₂ 0.50. ABG pH 7.30, PaCO₂ 43 mm Hg, PaO₂ 118 mm Hg, HCO₃ 22 mEq/L, base excess −6; lactate 4 mmol/L. CXR shows no edema or atelectasis. CVP 15 mm Hg and echocardiogram shows poor RV function. Which ventilator adjustment is MOST likely to improve RV performance?",
