    "scenario": "A 2-month-old infant is admitted to the PICU with prolonged fever, jaundice, lethargy, poor feeding, and a generalized maculopapular rash after a recent SARS-CoV-2 and rhinovirus infection. Cytopenias, hepatocellular injury, coagulopathy, high inflammatory markers, and low fibrinogen are present. Platelets are 10,000/µL, hemoglobin 8.8 g/dL, AST 497 U/L, ALT 251 U/L, ferritin 5,200 ng/mL, triglycerides 293 mg/dL, fibrinogen 50 mg/dL, and INR 1.9. Of the following, the BEST confirmatory test is",
