    "scenario": "A 14-year-old 60-kg adolescent with idiopathic juvenile scoliosis undergoes elective T2–L1 spinal fusion with 1.5 L intraoperative colloid and crystalloid. After surgery, she becomes lethargic with worsening headache and oliguria (0.2 mL/kg/h). She remains normotensive. Serum sodium is 124 mEq/L, serum osmolality 260 mOsm/kg, urine osmolality 500 mOsm/kg, and urine sodium 80 mEq/L. Of the following, the MOST likely cause of the electrolyte derangement is",
